gner_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"15da3d80e2b41646b21782f676f5176acd0743efcc8069e09639641d936e16d6","event_uuid":"1f7eb4f8-0abd-4e56-8250-3ab317339eeb","position":{"commit_sha":"8a72bebfba7e308a6d2a1dc5479d5dd8a3ef6671","position":"1788336943667014001-1f7eb4f8-0abd-4e56-8250-3ab317339eeb"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-258_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"b49fe82a-1778-4290-aefd-33d2684ae335","comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"AC3 evidence [non-codebase]. The 14 follow-up tickets exist and each carries an OUTBOUND discovered_from edge to this task. Verified child-side, because rebar deps on THIS task shows only its own outbound edges and cannot surface inbound ones — which is why AC3 is tagged [non-codebase] and why its original verification command was wrong.\n\nCommand, run against every child:\n  for t in <the 14 ids>; do rebar deps $t | grep discovered_from; done\nResult: 14 / 14 children carry the edge.\n\nThe 14, each proposing generate-or-gate for one genuine mirror from reports/stability/mirror-inventory.md:\n  545a-4db5-3a64-42d9  F1  reducer event-type dispatch (HIGH, silent data loss)\n  fd6b-09c5-8f76-45ad  F12 docs/exit-codes.md drifted + false gate claim (HIGH)\n  0d3c-ff25-5317-4d73  F13 code-review gate step ids unvalidated (HIGH)\n  62eb-5e6f-512a-420d  F5  MCP output models re-type canonical enums (HIGH)\n  e755-9371-7951-454a  F3  plan-review ticket-type exemption, six sites (HIGH)\n  cacb-8d57-efff-4ab1  F4  blocking/non-blocking relation partition (MEDIUM)\n  a691-f454-92c5-49bd  F10 three doc enumerations drifted (MEDIUM)\n  6850-af5c-a4a1-4c5d  F2  op-cert kinds, three masters (MEDIUM)\n  a516-e61b-ede9-465c  F6  TicketStatus re-declared in the reducer (MEDIUM)\n  ce8f-4da9-2836-4115  F7  TicketType re-declared on the create path (MEDIUM)\n  91b0-6185-b53c-4271  F8  CANONICAL_RELATIONS not pinned to the schema (LOW)\n  70f5-2253-1671-474d  F9  config precedence layers, two masters (LOW)\n  1daf-a435-2387-412c  F11 cross-session warn verb spellings (LOW)\n  0af1-44ec-0b47-4611  F14 the 17 mutating verbs, three masters (LOW)\nAll 14 are parented under epic undamaged-murderous-horse (f79d-0d71-0fd7-439f), which is linked\nrelates_to this epic's parent 87cb-7121-a3b6-4606.","timestamp":1788336943667014001}],"created_at":1788311498329604970,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"8c684632-2aa2-4d7c-ac16-8bf19e148cab","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"c333-02f8-8e16-4cd8"}],"description":"## Context\n\nRepresentation drift (a schema/set/surface and a hand-maintained copy diverging) is the dominant sub-mechanism of the product-logic defect category (R2S1). Three mirror classes are already generated/gated (config↔docs via `gen_config_reference.py`, env-vars↔docs via `gen_env_registry.py`, library surface via `gen_api_surface.py`); the terminal-status set was unified by bug e63c; the MCP↔library gap is sibling story `cream-capitate-snake` (8ce5-b870-601d-4715). This task finds what else remains — unknown mirrors are unknown defect sources.\n\n## Approach\n\nSystematic sweep of `src/rebar` for hand-maintained duplicates of a canonical fact: enumerations duplicated across modules (status-like sets, error-code lists, event-type lists), doc tables restating code constants, schema fragments re-declared, hardcoded path/name lists mirroring a registry. Method: grep/AST passes for duplicate literal sets, cross-referenced with schemas and generators; each candidate is verified as a genuine mirror (same fact, two masters) rather than a distinct concept (the e63c audit's claimability-vs-terminal distinction). Deliverable is an inventory with dispositions; fixes land as follow-up tickets, not in this task.\n\n`reports/` is currently gitignored (`.gitignore` `/reports/`), so committing the deliverable requires re-including the `reports/stability/` subtree. Git does not descend into an excluded directory, so the rule must become `/reports/*` plus a `!/reports/stability/` negation.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [x] AC1: `reports/stability/mirror-inventory.md` is committed, and lists every candidate examined with a verdict of `genuine mirror` / `distinct concept` / `already gated`. Verified by `git ls-files reports/stability/mirror-inventory.md` printing the path.\n- [x] AC2: every finding carries `file:line` evidence for at least two masters. Verified by reading the report: each genuine-mirror row cites two or more locations.\n- [x] AC3 [non-codebase]: every genuine live mirror has a linked ticket created `discovered_from` this task, proposing generate-or-gate using an existing repo pattern. The evidence lives in the ticket store, not the repository, and the link is recorded as an OUTBOUND `discovered_from` edge on each CHILD — so `rebar deps` on this task cannot show it. Verified per child instead, e.g. `rebar deps 545a-4db5-3a64-42d9`; the full list is in a comment on this ticket.\n- [x] AC4: the inventory states the sweep method (the exact grep/AST patterns searched, and candidates examined per area) so the sweep is repeatable by a later reader.\n- [x] AC5: the sibling story's mirror (MCP↔library) is referenced as already-filed, not re-filed as a new ticket.\n- [x] AC6: `reports/stability/` is committable — the `.gitignore` rule is changed to `/reports/*` plus `!/reports/stability/`, and no other previously-ignored `reports/` content becomes tracked. Verified by `git status --porcelain reports/` showing only the intended file, and `git check-ignore -v reports/` still ignoring the parent.\n\n## Testing\n\nThis task ships a report plus a one-line `.gitignore` change; its verification is the committed-artifact and link checks named in the acceptance criteria, run from the worktree:\n\n- `git ls-files reports/stability/mirror-inventory.md` — proves the deliverable is tracked (AC1) and that the `.gitignore` negation works (AC6).\n- `git status --porcelain reports/` — proves no unintended `reports/` content became tracked (AC6).\n- `rebar deps f9b9-83ad-931c-4833` — proves the `discovered_from` follow-up tickets exist and are linked (AC3).\n- `make lint` — proves the `.gitignore` edit breaks no existing gate (in particular the docs and deploy-manifest checks).\n\nNo new automated test is added: the change introduces no executable behavior, and the mechanism ratchet (sibling `unblacked-loveless-toad`) counts new gates rather than reports. A follow-up gate for any mirror found is scoped to that mirror's own ticket, not here.\n\n## File impact\n\n- `reports/stability/mirror-inventory.md` (new; committed inventory deliverable)\n- `.gitignore` (re-include `reports/stability/` so the deliverable can be committed)","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"reports/stability/mirror-inventory.md","reason":"committed inventory deliverable"},{"path":".gitignore","reason":"re-include reports/stability/ so the deliverable is committable (reports/ is currently ignored)"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["parent","87cb-7121-a3b6-4606"],["relates_to","c333-02f8-8e16-4cd8"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"87cb-7121-a3b6-4606","parent_status_uuid":"9530156c-b0a4-4a20-83fe-cba3d86fc909","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":["rebar"],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"f9b9-83ad-931c-4833","ticket_type":"task","title":"Representation-mirror inventory sweep: find and disposition remaining hand-maintained mirrors","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["2eef5921-9bd9-4570-bcc6-dd25333f821b","d083af68-c49b-430f-b1af-132382f4b178","39c96b98-8c38-4ac3-be90-98877219b2fd","b7b52887-36ba-4a3c-9f67-2e18c6a4c925","3aa9477f-fc86-4bc0-b603-659196648f8a","e6883317-6ea9-4546-8040-f07e572df64d","9530156c-b0a4-4a20-83fe-cba3d86fc909","4439f29b-7bb4-4e4e-8243-f01ae5752131","8c684632-2aa2-4d7c-ac16-8bf19e148cab","3276d982-aa89-4e6e-92cd-203597040fee","b25593d0-9be1-4d68-8f4e-62b32b44cd84","1f7eb4f8-0abd-4e56-8250-3ab317339eeb"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788336943667014002,"uuid":"450f06b3-f135-44b1-826c-767a93ce582c"}